    "statement": "The extremal branch canonically produces a nonzero biform G(t,X) of exact bidegree (e-2,p-3). For every classified noncore coordinate x, G(t,x) has e-2 distinct roots among the 3e off-line supported slopes, while at least e+6+d_A off-line fibers G(delta,X) have p-3 distinct roots in U_0 and are scalar multiples of their inside-support locators. The construction is the dual-GRS representation of the three-line-divided Hankel kernel equation.",
